<title>FRANCE: Algeria's leading novelist Benhadouga dies at 70.</title>
<headline>Algeria's leading novelist Benhadouga dies at 70.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's leading novelist Abdelhamid Benhadouga died on Monday after a chronic disease, the Algerian state-run television said. He was 70 years old.</p>
<p>Benhadouga is widely known at home and abroad for his rich literary works, including his Arab-language novels &quot;Rih al Janoub&quot; (South Wind) and &quot;Djaziya oua Darwish&quot;, a trilogy about Algeria history.</p>
</text>
